<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:52:19Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Sweden's centre-left opposition leads election as far-right slips, exit polls show</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c7ee596c32ec1250307b790dc703de94893134c9cbd646876e21335ebfe59f8</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:51:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T18:25:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-leads-election-as-far-right-slips-exit-polls-show--f5ea96e6c759.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-sweden-s-centre-left-opposition-leads-election-as-far-right-slips-exit-polls-show" /><summary type="html">Sweden's centre-left wing bloc, led by the Social Democrats, held an early lead at 51.3% in a parliamentary election on Sunday, an exit ​poll by broadcaster SVT ‌showed. Early results from the Swedish Election Authority were expected within hours.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden: Tight election puts all eyes on the far right</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c2090dc0ac1124a2f9d7775bfe2050ad35ec01bbff18c916fe152f51f80f80f</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:52:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T15:55:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sweden-tight-election-puts-all-eyes-on-the-far-right--e820006209b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-tight-election-puts-all-eyes-on-the-far-right" /><summary type="html">Swedes are voting in a closely fought general election that could see the far-right Sweden Democrats enter government for the first time. With immigration, crime and the economy dominating the campaign, Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson and Social Democrat leader Magdalena Andersson are locked in a neck-and-neck race.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI : 'We need to take the risk seriously and have more coordination'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:374d86e76dfa068810f1eccdc0e56e7bb46040215866b45302ad1a404309ed44</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:52:04Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T15:50:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ai-we-need-to-take-the-risk-seriously-and-have-more-coordination--cbbe2ec77e46.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ai-we-need-to-take-the-risk-seriously-and-have-more-coordination" /><summary type="html">This week's debate over AI has put the spotlight on how seriously we should take the technology's growing risks. On FRANCE 24, University of Salford Chair in Science Communication and Future Media, Andy Miah, argued that while AI poses real challenges requiring closer coordination between companies and governments, there is no existential threat to humanity. He also said clearer data and concrete figures would help the public better understand the risks.</summary></entry><entry><title>France's far-right Marine Le Pen kicks off 2027 presidential campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64f77dc53caa4f35bc78729e7f8a344ab7eceb763d4632c3499f8e17576e46a5</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:52:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T15:41:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france-s-far-right-marine-le-pen-kicks-off-2027-presidential-campaign--b14bc4e40ab8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france-s-far-right-marine-le-pen-kicks-off-2027-presidential-campaign" /><summary type="html">In France, Marine Le Pen has launched her presidential campaign with a rally in Hénin-Beaumont this Sunday, despite wearing an electronic tag following her recent conviction. On FRANCE 24, international affairs editor Oliver Farry explains why she remains the frontrunner in the polls despite her weakened legal position, pointing to her long-standing national profile, the appeal of her "national preference" agenda, and the left's struggle to unite behind a convincing candidate.</summary></entry><entry><title>The race to make AI safer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a25b8e5f6ead6916e47ebf9ee9555e3b2cab2da89dba5e548496f0e78406a620</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:52:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T15:16:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/the-race-to-make-ai-safer--16f2e6906bd7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/the-race-to-make-ai-safer" /><summary type="html">As AI leaders warn that the technology is advancing faster than our ability to control it, Donald Trump has dismissed some of those concerns as exaggerated. On FRANCE 24, AI philosophy professor Raphaël Millière said this summer's real-world AI security incident shows the risks are no longer hypothetical, while stressing that it does not mean "AI will kill us all". Instead, he argues the priority is coordinated action by companies and governments to manage increasingly real safety risks.</summary></entry><entry><title>Surfing: France tests Olympic venue ahead of LA 2028</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf647b7ef75f55f916ef010eb89d92393b5280d00ad68c32fc1c646229c8fa92</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:52:13Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T15:04:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/surfing-france-tests-olympic-venue-ahead-of-la-2028--05a6e3d0ee0e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/surfing-france-tests-olympic-venue-ahead-of-la-2028" /><summary type="html">With the Lexus Trestles Pro underway in California, the French surfing team is using the future Los Angeles 2028 Olympic venue for its first full-scale training camp. Led by reigning Olympic champion Kauli Vaast, the squad is testing both its sporting preparation and team logistics as it builds towards defending France's medal success from Paris 2024.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: The Houthis test Iran's regional influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d7156225de6c0fdb5d005a27bb95740b779e9a4535cf67d755c4d8228b2ac39</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:52:16Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:29:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-yemen-the-houthis-test-iran-s-regional-influence--7c06853f246c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-yemen-the-houthis-test-iran-s-regional-influence" /><summary type="html">Iran-backed Houthi attacks on Saudi Arabia have intensified as fighting spreads around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, a vital chokepoint for global trade and oil shipments. On FRANCE 24, Sanaa Center for Strategic Studies chairman Farea Al-Muslimi argued this could mark "the last round in Yemen's current war", unpacking the Houthis' ties with Iran and the growing pressure on Washington as the group targets US allies while Donald Trump heads into a crucial election.</summary></entry><entry><title>Indonesia: Second ferry disaster in five days</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5b19f8b8af8f16a8b50d5b664cf3492c9827b3d42acc9ad621a40a35852fe418</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:17:21Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days--bcdea8ab2589.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/indonesia-second-ferry-disaster-in-five-days" /><summary type="html">At least one person has died and more than 100 people remain missing after a ferry carrying 243 people sank in rough weather between the Indonesian islands of Java and Borneo. The disaster is the second major ferry accident in the region in five days, renewing concerns over safety standards, overcrowding and maintenance.</summary></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Fighting escalates around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ff24e1dc829daea5d95a48aea186519b46cda5e5ff5d009cf469d046dd1e09a</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:15:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait--7a2aac2b3186.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-fighting-escalates-around-the-bab-el-mandeb-strait" /><summary type="html">Fighting is escalating in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi forces seized strategic territory around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, prompting counterstrikes by government forces and reported Saudi air raids. The Houthis also claimed attacks inside southern Saudi Arabia and threatened to disrupt shipping through the key maritime chokepoint, raising fears for regional security and global trade.</summary></entry><entry><title>Swedish far-right eyes role in government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c6f833a2095ad4b52765869c975d17d0f451c19fb464a381fe9bc18f238742a6</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T13:11:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government--89cf8fdd015f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/swedish-far-right-eyes-role-in-government" /><summary type="html">As Sweden heads into a closely fought election, the far right is gaining ground by tapping into concerns over crime and security, issues that some voters increasingly associate with migration. On FRANCE 24, Stockholm University sociologist Zeth Isaksson said the movement has also softened its image in recent years, making it more acceptable to a broader electorate, while also cautioning against overstating the strength of the far right in Sweden.</summary></entry><entry><title>Radio France staff strike over appointment of far-right weekly editor</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c773c5c820e0b66f7cc05608b92abba0f7a471be12ec286e2b3cc1dbb2260a8f</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T12:44:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-radio-france-staff-strike-over-appointment-of-far-right-weekly-editor--07059883adf7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-radio-france-staff-strike-over-appointment-of-far-right-weekly-editor" /><summary type="html">Staff at public broadcaster Radio France began a two-day strike on Sunday over the appointment of Charles Sapin, deputy editor-in-chief at far-right weekly Valeurs Actuelles. Unions accuse Sapin of promoting far-right ideas ahead of next spring's presidential election, while management has defended the appointment in the name of pluralism.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Brazil: Michelle Bolsonaro's key role in the presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0d12e1f1f464ca0c7545704a91c18d777b892a41b8180838dd5dbe640f824bb</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T11:08:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race--c6d331e45ad7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-michelle-bolsonaro-s-key-role-in-the-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">Brazil is heading to the polls on October 4, with President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva seeking a fourth term as the Bolsonaro family mounts a political comeback through Flávio's presidential bid and Michelle's Senate campaign. With polls pointing to another tight race, Michelle's popularity among women could prove crucial as the family tries to return to power.</summary></entry><entry><title>The week in pictures: 9/11 anniversary, far-right win in Germany and Houthis' Yemen offensive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4258174492f443055773c92874eecd1d104423531bb5b66fb7963e42c689b77a</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T10:48:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive--652ff4e85a45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-the-week-in-pictures-9-11-anniversary-far-right-win-germany-houthis-yemen-offensive" /><summary type="html">A look back at some of the week's key news stories and the most striking images, from commemorations marking 25 years since the 9/11 attacks to the breakthrough win for Germany's far-right AfD party and the lightening offensive that has left Yemen's Iran-backed Houthi rebels in control of the country's Red Sea coast.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Sweden election: A turning point for the far right?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8720261729347ff113adc54b0b3c63572f41a0050eeaf75141ef8cdabb701c90</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:48:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right--20fbe48330d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sweden-election-a-turning-point-for-the-far-right" /><summary type="html">The stakes are high in Sweden's general election, with the far right poised to enter government for the first time. TV4 News journalist Markus Karlsson-Bourrioux explains how opinion polls shifted from a comfortable centre-left lead to a tight race over the summer, and how far-right ideas have gained ground since the last election in 2022.</summary></entry><entry><title>Germany: Thousands rally against far-right after AfD victory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4a5be92b03592d6f497080773c193db331d6047f9a59a8998c3230f58972f690</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:41:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory--38396b69fe17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/germany-thousands-rally-against-far-right-after-afd-victory" /><summary type="html">Tens of thousands of people marched in around 20 cities across Germany to protest the rise of the far right after the AfD's historic victory in the Saxony-Anhalt state election. Demonstrators said they were defending democracy as mainstream parties continue to rule out governing with the AfD.</summary></entry><entry><title>BRICS summit: What came out of the New Delhi meeting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cc4102651506479c59f87e97262968b17b16c4302497638f2653bf69edd802b</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:27:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/brics-summit-what-came-out-of-the-new-delhi-meeting--2d7ab6cb6280.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/brics-summit-what-came-out-of-the-new-delhi-meeting" /><summary type="html">The BRICS summit in New Delhi ended with a joint declaration calling for greater Global South influence in global governance and urging restraint in the Middle East. The gathering also served as a platform for one-to-one diplomacy, with leaders holding a series of bilateral meetings aimed at easing regional tensions. FRANCE 24's Navodita Kumari has the details.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK: Police probe £72 million donation to Reform UK</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cd9df9eef5d4ec7f09dc2012f1ca6ba1f6211988caef49ef988f37a9bd06eb2</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:26:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-uk-police-probe-_72-million-donation-to-reform-uk--7eb204a7eff8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260913-uk-police-probe-%C2%A372-million-donation-to-reform-uk" /><summary type="html">British police have opened a criminal investigation into a £72 million donation to Nigel Farage's Reform UK, amid questions over whether the funds breached rules on foreign political donations. The probe comes as anti-immigration protests and counter-demonstrations intensify across England, highlighting growing tensions over immigration and national identity.</summary></entry><entry><title>Macron, Carney to visit North Atlantic French islands after Trump's map post</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0f60915ec802880af384351d8a7271bdbc52f65b204583667b85478c47fc543</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:25:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post--f17f71093187.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260913-macron-carney-to-visit-french-islands-after-trump-s-map-post" /><summary type="html">French President Emmanuel Macron and Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney will reaffirm the “sovereignty of nations” on a visit on September 20 to Saint-Pierre-et-Miquelon, a French territory in the North Atlantic, the Élysée Palace announced on Sunday. The symbolic trip comes after US President Donald Trump posted a map on social media showing the entire North American continent covered by the US flag.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthi offensive triggers new displacement crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef053cddf148d32e3d984cd326f36243a95aec7df65dc80056c62db9d489856a</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:18:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-houthi-offensive-triggers-new-displacement-crisis--2ca71fdc0d39.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-houthi-offensive-triggers-new-displacement-crisis" /><summary type="html">More than 70,000 people have fled their homes in Yemen after Iran-backed Houthi rebels launched an offensive to seize the Bab el-Mandeb Strait, with many escaping to Aden and around 1,400 crossing into neighbouring Djibouti. The UN and IOM warn the new displacement wave is worsening an already dire humanitarian crisis in a country devastated by 12 years of war.</summary></entry><entry><title>France apologises for diplomatic spat with US to lift block on new ambassador to Washington</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:efe00f3abcbd37c9d39aa9ebf3df57d695b63d1f2f8099b699efd6818cdbe1f7</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T09:01:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-france-apologises-for-diplomatic-spat-with-us-to-lift-block-on-new-ambassador-to-washington--6f9350753c15.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20260913-france-apologises-for-diplomatic-spat-with-us-to-lift-block-on-new-ambassador-to-washington" /><summary type="html">The French UN mission said it regretted an online post criticising a US vote at the UN General Assembly in a move that should clear the way for the new French ambassador Aurélien Lechevallier to take up his post in Washington.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Trump slams AI sceptics as Altman pauses OpenAI IPO plans over safety concerns</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:12eb2b173a6e3732c0eace1ad263918040c662bdda563886d46ec94b6370e140</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:52:19Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T08:23:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/technology/20260913-trump-slams-ai-skeptics-as-altman-pauses-openai-ipo-plans-over-safety-concerns--1ac4e3183f58.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/technology/20260913-trump-slams-ai-skeptics-as-altman-pauses-openai-ipo-plans-over-safety-concerns" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Sunday slammed critics of artificial intelligence (AI) who warned firms to slow down development, branding them "negative" forces. The comments came soon after OpenAI CEO Sam Altman announced his company will not go public this year, citing safety concerns.</summary><category term="Technology" /></entry><entry><title>On Sept 12th, 'everyone was compassionate': The world needs 'to be together again' - Richard Roeill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4528fd4975498a477216b45a7a55c078463d64284dfbc0678033d0e88f3ca38</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T07:18:22Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill--bad1381d87fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260913-on-sept-12th-everyone-was-compassionate-the-world-needs-to-be-together-again-richard-roeill" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome Richard Roeill, former New York Firefighter and 9/11 First Responder. His testimony reframes the legacy of September 11th not as a historical event confined to a single day, but as living history. The former New York City firefighter describes an anniversary that reactivates trauma, while the illnesses suffered by first responders make the consequences of Ground Zero ever present decades later. Yet Roeill’s testimony is not simply a narrative of sacrifice. He says that responders were misled about the dangers they faced, demanding accountability and long-term healthcare for those exposed to the very toxic air.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Olympic rematch: US and France to meet for women's FIBA World Cup title</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:09179304551f0f6eb443d9a0f01b662c80c7d31f270e0e1d39dceefdbcf0a2e9</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T06:48:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20260913-olympic-rematch-us-and-france-to-meet-for-women-s-fiba-world-cup-title--4ae45ec08999.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20260913-olympic-rematch-us-and-france-to-meet-for-women-s-fiba-world-cup-title" /><summary type="html">France won against host Germany in the women's FIBA World Cup semifinals Saturday and will now face the United States in the final Sunday after the four-time defending champion and tournament favorite defeated Spain in the other semifinal.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>Swedes vote in close general election that could usher far right into government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c36c5b143f27c462c6d0c2a6f0a59090bf70121bbbab1f409a6f4d91d7d14abb</id><updated>2026-09-13T18:50:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-13T06:16:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government--c14a0b3c76df.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20260913-swedes-vote-in-close-general-election-that-could-usher-far-right-into-government" /><summary type="html">Swedes are heading to the polls Sunday for a general election that will either bring a far right party into government for the first time or shift the country back towards the liberalism it has long been known for. The centre-left opposition holds a narrow lead over the ruling right-wing bloc but Prime ⁠Minister Ulf Kristersson's four-party alliance – which includes the far right Sweden Democrats – has been catching up in the final weeks of campaigning.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry></feed>
